"""
    variation_by_accession(accession; sourcetype, consequencetype, wildtype, alternativesequence, location, accept = :json)

Get natural variants by UniProt accession

Among the available response content types, PEFF format (PSI Extended FASTA Format from the Human Proteome Organisation - Proteomics Standards Initiative, HUPO-PSI) is provided with only variants reported in the output.

`GET /variation/{accession}` (operationId `getVariation`, tag `variation`)

# Arguments
- `accession::AbstractString` (spec: string; pattern `([O,P,Q][0-9][A-Z|0-9]{3}[0-9]|[A-N,R-Z]([0-9][A-Z][A-Z|0-9]{2}){1,2}[0-9])(-\\d+)*`)

# Query parameters
- `sourcetype::ListParam` (spec: string; pattern `^(uniprot|large scale study|mixed|clinvar|nci-tcga|cosmic curated|ensembl|gnomad|topmed|exac)(,(uniprot|large scale study|mixed|clinvar|nci-tcga|cosmic curated|ensembl|gnomad|topmed|exac))*\$`): Filter by the sourceType for variants: uniprot, large scale study, mixed, clinvar, nci-tcga, cosmic curated, ensembl, gnomad, topmed and exac. Comma separated values accepted up to 2.
- `consequencetype::ListParam` (spec: string; pattern `^(missense|stop\\sgained|stop\\slost)(,(missense|stop\\sgained|stop\\slost))*\$`): Filter by consequenceType for variants: missense, stop gained or stop lost. Comma separated values accepted up to 2.
- `wildtype::ListParam` (spec: string; pattern `^[A-Za-z\\-]{1,20}(,[A-Za-z\\-]{1,20})*\$`): Search by specific wildType amino acid. Options: Any single letter amino acid and * for stop codon. Comma separated values accepted up to 20.
- `alternativesequence::ListParam` (spec: string; pattern `^[A-Za-z\\-]{1,20}(,[A-Za-z\\-]{1,20})*\$`): Filter by the alternativeSequence amino acid. Any single letter amino acid and * for stopcodon and - for deletions. Comma separated values accepted up to 20.
- `location::AbstractString` (spec: string): Filter by the amino acid range position in the sequence(s). Any valid amino acid range position within the length of the protein sequence such as 10-60 (start position to end position)

# Response
Formats listed in the spec: `application/json`.
JSON schema: `ProteinFeatureInfo`.
See `EBIProteinsRestClient` for `accept` and the `VariationByAccessionEndpoint` struct.
"""
@endpoint struct VariationByAccessionEndpoint <: EBIEndpoint
    variation_by_accession(accession) -> "variation/{_value(self.accession)}?sourcetype={_value(self.sourcetype)}&consequencetype={_value(self.consequencetype)}&wildtype={_value(self.wildtype)}&alternativesequence={_value(self.alternativesequence)}&location={_value(self.location)}" -> _responsetype(self)
    accession::AbstractString
